ng despite vocal imperfections.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-04-08T14:50:58.000Z"},{"id":"R3KjhQnKm","title":"Smashing Meets Modern CSS","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/smashing-meets-modern-css/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/smashing-meets-modern-css-r3kjhqnkm","summary":"Geoff Graham hosted a panel discussion on modern CSS with three experts: Miriam discussed the intersection of author, user, and user agent styles; Julia shared innovative uses of animations for microinteractions; Adam demonstrated new CSS features through an array of demos.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-04-07T17:05:21.000Z"},{"id":"fK1Fixxjr","title":"Open Up With Brad Frost: Episode 1","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/open-up-with-brad-frost-episode-1/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/open-up-with-brad-frost-episode-1-fk1fixxjr","summary":"Open Up is a new podcast co-hosted by Geoff Graham and Brad Frost, focusing on the emotional aspects of working in tech and web development. The first episode covers topics like job layoffs, lack of purpose at work, and more, with Brad offering empathetic and practical insights. The podcast is interactive, encouraging audience participation in live episodes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qPvKM23u--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2009","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-19T16:14:42.000Z"},{"id":"8xDgGZ306","title":"If someone asks me to do something \u201ckindly\u201d I often find myself fighting the urge to exercise a little indirect malice. You know, just to spite.","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/if-someone-asks-me-to-do-something-kindly-i-often-find-myself-fighting-the-urge-to-exercise-a-little-indirect-malice-you-know-just-to-spite/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/if-someone-asks-me-to-do-something-kindly-i-often-find-myself-fighting-the-urge-to-exercise-a-litt-8xdggz306","summary":"The author describes feeling a strong urge to perform a small act of malice when asked to do something politely, highlighting a spiteful reaction to the word 'kindly'.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-19T15:50:29.000Z"},{"id":"4nE7WwQWx","title":"I judge podcasts and videos on whether they offer a 1.75\u00d7 speed option. That\u2019s my baby bear porridge right there.","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/i-judge-podcasts-and-videos-on-whether-they-offer-a-1-75x-speed-option-thats-my-baby-bear-porridge-right-there/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-judge-podcasts-and-videos-on-whether-they-offer-a-1-75-speed-option-that-s-my-baby-bear-porridge-4ne7wwqwx","summary":"The author prefers to consume podcasts and videos at a playback speed of 1.75\u00d7, finding it the ideal pace for efficient content consumption.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-13T17:11:16.000Z"},{"id":"wsK4mXNlM","title":"I just migrated two sites from PHP 7 to 8 and boy are my feet tired.","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/i-just-migrated-two-sites-from-php-7-to-8-and-boy-are-my-feet-tired/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-just-migrated-two-sites-from-php-7-to-8-and-boy-are-my-feet-tired--wsk4mxnlm","summary":"The author shares their experience of migrating two websites from PHP 7 to PHP 8. The process involved updating the codebase to ensure compatibility with the latest version and handling any issues that arose during the migration. The transition aimed to leverage the improvements and new features introduced in PHP 8.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-02-12T17:29:38.000Z"},{"id":"7ElQzwTS0","title":"\u201cThis monophonic microgroove recording is playable on monophonic and stereo phonographs. It cannot become obsolete. It will continue to be a source of outstanding sound reproduction, providing the fin","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/this-monophonic-microgroove-recording-is-playable-on-monophonic-and-stereo-phonographs-it-cannot-become-obsolete-it-will-continue-to-be-a-source-of-outstanding-sound-reproduction-providing-the-fi/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/this-monophonic-microgroove-recording-is-playable-on-monophonic-and-stereo-phonographs-it-cannot-b-7elqzwts0","summary":"Monophonic microgroove recordings are designed to be compatible with both monophonic and stereo phonographs. These recordings ensure outstanding sound reproduction and are immune to becoming obsolete, delivering the finest monophonic performance on any phonograph.","image":"https://i0.wp.com/geoffgraham.me/wp-content/uploads/IMG_2608.jpeg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-14T19:55:53.000Z"},{"id":"KwYPKeHOz","title":"Addition by Omission","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/addition-by-omission/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/addition-by-omission-kwypkehoz","summary":"A hidden profanity in the Beatles' 'Hey Jude' at the 2:58 mark serves as an example of how imperfections can add value to music. This seven-minute song, which held a record for nine weeks at Number 1 in the U.S. in 1968, includes Paul McCartney swearing over a botched piano chord, something that would likely be edited out in modern productions. The Beatles' approach to such quirks, including inaudible high-pitch tones for pets in 'Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band,' highlights how intentional omissions and imperfections can make music more memorable.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--P4t4XyoV--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2001","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-07T16:27:30.000Z"},{"id":"XNQ8rTlyQ","title":"I looked for a WordPress alternative to teach framework development next semester and landed on Astro. Wow, it\u2019s a lot of fun and I can\u2019t wait to do the lectures!","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/i-looked-for-a-wordpress-alternative-to-teach-framework-development-next-semester-and-landed-on-astro-wow-its-a-lot-of-fun-and-i-cant-wait-to-do-the-lectures/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-looked-for-a-wordpress-alternative-to-teach-framework-development-next-semester-and-landed-on-astr-xnq8rtlyq","summary":"Astro, an alternative to WordPress, is being explored for teaching framework development. The author finds Astro enjoyable to use and is excited about using it for lectures.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--58gMhC4P--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2012","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-20T19:18:45.000Z"},{"id":"1H6FS5MEs","title":"The Next Beatles Album","url":"https://geoffgraham.me/the-next-beatles-album/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-next-beatles-album-1h6fs5mes","summary":"The post imagines a hypothetical Beatles album had they stayed together beyond 1970-71, using solo tracks from John, Paul, George, and Ringo. It details a potential tracklist, giving reasons for the inclusion of songs like 'Imagine' and 'Maybe I'm Amazed,' while considering the dynamics and contributions of each member.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qPvKM23u--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2009","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-12T21:42:11.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["tripleb","twosixtech","rosindustrial","jimmybogard","equinix"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","horde","on_leuwcq","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"tripleb","handle":"tripleb","name":"Triplebyte","is_squad":fa